{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++ code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++ code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n#define mod 1000000007\ntypedef unsigned long long int LL;\nstruct M{\n    LL s[35][35],n;\n    friend M operator * (M a,M b){\n        M c;\n        c.n=a.n;\n        int i,j,k;\n        for(i=0;i<a.n;i++){\n            for(j=0;j<a.n;j++){\n                c.s[i][j]=0;\n                for(k=0;k<a.n;k++){\n                    c.s[i][j]+=a.s[i][k]*b.s[k][j];\n                    c.s[i][j]%=mod;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return c;\n    }\n}bi[65][65],I;\nint main(){\n    LL n,m,t,x,y,z,add;\n    int i,j,k;\n    scanf(\"%llu%llu\",&n,&m);\n    bi[0][0].n=m+1;\n    for(i=0;i<=m;i++){\n        bi[0][0].s[i][i]=1;\n        bi[0][0].s[0][i]=1;\n    }\n    x=0,y=1,z=0,add=0;\n    while(y*m<=n){\n        y*=m;\n        x++;\n    }\n    for(t=0;t<=x;t++){\n        if(t){\n            bi[t][0]=bi[t-1][0];\n            for(i=1;i<m;i++){\n                bi[t][0]=bi[t][0]*bi[t-1][i];\n            }\n        }\n        for(i=1;i<m;i++){\n            bi[t][i]=bi[t][i-1];\n            for(j=m-2;j>=0;j--){\n                for(k=0;k<=m;k++){\n                    swap(bi[t][i].s[j][k],bi[t][i].s[j+1][k]);\n                }\n            }\n            for(j=m-2;j>=0;j--){\n                for(k=0;k<=m;k++){\n                    swap(bi[t][i].s[k][j],bi[t][i].s[k][j+1]);\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n    }\n    for(i=0;i<=m;i++){\n        I.n=m+1;\n        I.s[i][i]=1;\n    }\n    while(add<n){\n        //printf(\"%llu\",add);\n        if(add<=n-y){\n            add+=y;\n            I=I*bi[x][z];\n            z=(z+1)%m;\n        }\n        else{\n            y/=m;\n            x--;\n        }\n    }\n    //I.pt();\n    LL ans=0;\n    for(i=0;i<=m;i++){\n        ans=(ans+I.s[i][m])%mod;\n    }\n    printf(\"%llu\\n\",ans);\n}\n\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\n\nmod = 1000000007\n\nclass Matrix:\n    def __init__(self, n):\n        self.n = n\n        self.s = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n    \n    def __mul__(self, other):\n        c = Matrix(self.n)\n        for i in range(self.n + 1):\n            for j in range(self.n + 1):\n                c.s[i][j] = 0\n                for k in range(self.n + 1):\n                    c.s[i][j] += self.s[i][k] * other.s[k][j]\n                    c.s[i][j] %= mod\n        return c\n\ndef main():\n    data = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    if not data:\n        return\n    n = int(data[0])\n    m = int(data[1])\n    \n    # Initialize bi array\n    bi = {}\n    for i in range(65):\n        for j in range(65):\n            bi[(i, j)] = Matrix(m)\n    \n    # Initialize bi[0][0]\n    bi[(0, 0)].n = m\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        bi[(0, 0)].s[i][i] = 1\n        bi[(0, 0)].s[0][i] = 1\n    \n    x = 0\n    y = 1\n    z = 0\n    add = 0\n    \n    while y * m <= n:\n        y *= m\n        x += 1\n    \n    for t in range(x + 1):\n        if t:\n            bi[(t, 0)] = bi[(t - 1, 0)]\n            for i in range(1, m):\n                bi[(t, 0)] = bi[(t, 0)] * bi[(t - 1, i)]\n        \n        for i in range(1, m):\n            bi[(t, i)] = bi[(t, i - 1)]\n            # Swap rows\n            for j in range(m - 1, -1, -1):\n                for k in range(m + 1):\n                    bi[(t, i)].s[j][k], bi[(t, i)].s[j + 1][k] = bi[(t, i)].s[j + 1][k], bi[(t, i)].s[j][k]\n            # Swap columns\n            for j in range(m - 1, -1, -1):\n                for k in range(m + 1):\n                    bi[(t, i)].s[k][j], bi[(t, i)].s[k][j + 1] = bi[(t, i)].s[k][j + 1], bi[(t, i)].s[k][j]\n    \n    # Initialize identity matrix I\n    I = Matrix(m)\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        I.s[i][i] = 1\n    \n    while add < n:\n        if add <= n - y:\n            add += y\n            I = I * bi[(x, z)]\n            z = (z + 1) % m\n        else:\n            y //= m\n            x -= 1\n    \n    ans = 0\n    for i in range(m + 1):\n        ans = (ans + I.s[i][m]) % mod\n    \n    print(ans)\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.75\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-0.0001734344696160406, -8.344646857949556e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -0.19765417277812958, -0.0004936429904773831, -1.4066597032069694e-05, -0.035845834761857986, -1.0728830375228426e-06, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0021858150139451027, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.00015901254664640874, -0.08905385434627533, -0.012584914453327656, -8.940656698541716e-06, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -2.264974000354414e-06, -3.4570634852570947e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -4.768370445162873e-07, -8.856858039507642e-05, -0.47425201535224915, -0.33754879236221313, -3.099436753473128e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -5.960462772236497e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -3.576278118089249e-07, -5.960446742392378e-06, -0